WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.535
-Well, good news, you guys.
Today is National Tequila Day.

00:00:03.535 --> 00:00:06.372
Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.372 --> 00:00:08.908
And after six hours of Robert
Mueller testifying,

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.177
I think we all deserve it.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:13.580
Doble, por favor.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:15.481
Actually, I saw that a lot
of bars in Washington

00:00:15.481 --> 00:00:18.117
opened at 8:00 a.m. this morning
for the Mueller hearings.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.952
If you did a shot any time
Mueller said

00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:22.354
"I can't answer that," you were
blacked out by 10:00 a.m.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:23.389
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:26.392
"I'm getting redacted today,
man."

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.228
That's right. It was a big event
on Capitol Hill.

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:30.162
Three months after
he released his report,

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:32.531
Mueller went to Congress
to answer some tough questions

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:33.966
about his investigation.

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.702
I don't want to say watching it
was draining,

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:38.304
but by the end, every American
looked like Robert Mueller.

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:42.975
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:44.710
Let's talk about the hearings,
though.

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:45.979
They were pretty intense.

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:49.849
Mueller was questioned by 60
lawmakers for six hours.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.384
The only other time
you get grilled like that

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:53.953
is if you're single
at your famry reunion.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:00:56.423
[ Laughter ]
Famry rerunion. Family reunion.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.824
Gosh!

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.359
You think that's funny, man?

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.693
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.395
Unbelievable. Unbelievable.
You think that's funny.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.264
That's the first joke you
laughed at all night, man.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.565
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:07.600
Famry --

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.368
Family reunion.
-Fammy reunion.

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:10.370
-[ Mumbling ]

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:11.671
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.671 --> 00:01:13.907
It's almost like I was playing
my record backwards.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:15.741
[ Mumbling ]

00:01:15.741 --> 00:01:18.310
Family rerunion.
Family rerunion.

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.712
Famry rerunion.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.781
[ Imitating record scratching ]

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.317
♪♪

00:01:24.317 --> 00:01:26.052
No.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:29.622
No. It's terrible.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.658
It's like Sylvester Stallone
doing the monologue.

00:01:32.658 --> 00:01:34.727
[ As Stallone ] Fammy weunion.
Fammy reuyun.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:39.465
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:41.234
I just had a family reunion.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.903
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.505
[ Normal voice ]
But the fireworks started early.

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:47.507
Mueller said the reason
that he couldn't charge Trump

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.375
with a crime was because
he can't indict

00:01:49.375 --> 00:01:51.010
a sitting president.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.645
That's why for the last 12
hours,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.213
Trump's been afraid
to get up from the couch.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:59.552
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.654
That's right. Mueller said that
Trump couldn't get indicted

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.922
because he's in office.

00:02:02.922 --> 00:02:04.423
But the president
is not out of the woods yet.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:05.625
Listen to this.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.660
-Could you charge the president
with a crime

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.996
after he left office?
-Yes.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:11.431
-Hmm.
[ Audience oohs ]

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:14.467
So Trump could be charged after
he's done being president.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.502
Right now in Russia, Putin's
looking at his phone like,

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:19.005
[ Russian accent ]
"Any second now.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.640
Hello, Donald. Yes, I can help."

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.574
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.574 --> 00:02:23.943
A lot of people are focusing on

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.611
all the things
Mueller didn't say.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.813
Instead of talking,
he just kept telling lawmakers

00:02:27.813 --> 00:02:29.648
to go back and read his report.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.450
Then the lawmakers were like,
"the whole point of us

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.552
bringing you here was so that we
didn't have to read the report.

00:02:33.552 --> 00:02:35.020
Come on, talk!"

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.489
That's right. Mueller avoided
a lot of questions.

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.024
Take a look at this.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.893
-I'm not going to get into what
we may or may not have included.

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:44.363
I'm not going to speculate.
That's beyond my purview.

00:02:44.363 --> 00:02:48.067
That was outside our purview.
That's not in my purview.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:50.169
-Yeah.
He's like a magic 8-ball,

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:51.871
except no matter how you shake
him, he just says,

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:52.905
"That's not in my purview."

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.239
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.239 --> 00:02:56.142
A lot of people in the media
are saying that Mueller

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.011
came across as old and slow.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.812
On the bright side,
he's now the favorite

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.714
to win the Democratic nomination
for president.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:02.915
[ Laughter ]
That's pretty good.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:07.086
[ Applause ]

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.621
But I really can't blame Mueller
for having trouble keeping up.

00:03:09.621 --> 00:03:11.423
Listen to what happened
when these first Republican

00:03:11.423 --> 00:03:12.958
promised to talk slowly.

00:03:12.958 --> 00:03:15.461
-I'll talk slowly.
I'm said that I talk fast.

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:16.729
I will talk slowly.

00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.330
Your report states that
your investigative team

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:20.900
included 19 lawyers
and approximately 40 FBI agents

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.502
and analysts and accountants.
Are those numbers accurate?

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:25.471
-Could you repeat that, please?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:28.307
-Is it also true that you issued
over 2,800 subpoenas,

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.108
executed nearly 500 search
warrants,

00:03:30.108 --> 00:03:32.611
obtained more than 230 orders
for communication records

00:03:32.611 --> 00:03:34.147
and 50 pin registers?

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.415
-That went a little fast for me.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:36.949
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.949 --> 00:03:38.784
-Oh, my goodness.

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:40.820
That's like being interviewed
by an auctioneer.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.554
It's like, "Hey, we're going to
start the bidding at 19 lawyers,

00:03:42.554 --> 00:03:44.590
40 FBI agents --
[ Calling ]

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:45.658
Going once, going twice!

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.360
Sold to the gentleman
in the back!"

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.561
If that guy did
all the questioning,

00:03:48.561 --> 00:03:50.530
the hearing would have been over
in six minutes.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.731
A lot of people laughed at this.

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.399
At one point,
Mueller had a little trouble

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.301
with the president's name.
Watch this.

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:58.103
-Did your investigation find
that the Russian government

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:02.475
perceived it would benefit from
one of the candidates winning?

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:03.842
-Yes.

00:04:03.842 --> 00:04:07.647
-And which candidate
would that be?

00:04:07.647 --> 00:04:09.982
-Well, it would be Trimp --
uh, Trump.

00:04:09.982 --> 00:04:11.483
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:13.051
-Then Trump was like,

00:04:13.051 --> 00:04:15.021
[ As Trump ] "See,
it was Trimp who obstructed.

00:04:15.021 --> 00:04:15.888
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:18.458
Not Trump, Trimp.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:20.759
Lock him up.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:24.096
Lock up Trimp."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.096 --> 00:04:26.732
The clip went viral,
which explains this yard sign

00:04:26.732 --> 00:04:28.701
I saw today --
Trimp-Pince, 2020.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:29.769
-Wow!

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:31.503
-Yeah, he changed his name.

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:34.173
-Pince.
-After the testimony,

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:36.009
both sides tried to declare
victory.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.743
And Trump sent out a tweet
that said,

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:39.945
"Truth is a force of nature."

00:04:39.945 --> 00:04:41.780
People were like,
"Wow, that's deep."

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:44.016
And Trump was like, "Thanks,
I got it from a fortune cookie."

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:45.551
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.319
If you missed Mueller's hearing,
don't worry.

00:04:47.319 --> 00:04:49.321
In a few weeks, William Barr
will give a much shorter,

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:51.591
inaccurate summary. Um...
[ Scattered laughter ]

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.126
You didn't like that joke?
It's okay.

00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:54.694
You don't have to like 'em all.
-Come on, that was a good joke.

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:55.661
-You don't have to like
all of them.

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:56.729
It's okay.
-That's a good joke!

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.164
-But after all the hype
and questioning,

00:04:58.164 --> 00:04:59.832
I don't think anybody's changed
their mind about anything.

00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:01.834
Democrats are still thinking
about impeachment.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.636
Republicans are still
saying case closed.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:05.638
America hasn't been this divided
since the trailer

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:07.140
for the "Cats" movie came out.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.608
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:11.277
One of the Republicans laying
into Mueller the most today

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.645
was Mike Johnson.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:14.146
This is interesting,
Mike Johnson --

00:05:14.146 --> 00:05:16.482
-Excuse me, Mr. Fallon,

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.983
what did you mean when you said

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:22.755
America hasn't been this divided
since the "Cats" trailer?

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:25.124
-I'm sorry, Higgins, what?

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.927
-Earlier joke, you stated,
and I quote,

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:30.696
"America hasn't been
this divided

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:32.598
since the 'Cats' trailer
came out."

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.866
Can you elaborate on that?

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:35.601
-I'm sorry, which -- which joke?

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:39.839
-I'm referring to cue card 12,
joke 3-A.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:43.542
"'Cats' trailer came out."
Explain what you meant, please.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:46.044
-What -- No, I'm not going to
explain the joke.

00:05:46.044 --> 00:05:47.813
You can just --

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.449
-Refer to your earlier
monologue. Yeah, I thought --

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:52.151
We thought you'd say that.
Anyway. Next --

00:05:52.151 --> 00:05:55.688
-Who is we?
-Next question.

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:59.858
Do you recall a joke, February
2013,

00:05:59.858 --> 00:06:01.961
where the punch line was,
and I quote,

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:04.597
"Chicken chalupa?"

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:07.433
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.235
-Chicken chalupa?
I mean, maybe I --

00:06:10.235 --> 00:06:12.805
-And what did you mean by that?

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:14.841
-It was 2013, Higgins.
I don't remember.

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:17.310
-What did you mean, Mr. Fallon?!

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.445
Chicken chalupa!

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.113
-That's out of my purview.
-Hey!

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:22.982
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:26.852
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.852 --> 00:06:29.755
It's my time!

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:31.357
You shut your cute mouth.

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:34.727
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:39.031
Final question --

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:42.601
June 18, 2019.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.370
You said, and I quote,

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.605
"Without Fox News,

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:48.107
Trump's only source of news
is Snapple caps."

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:52.144
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:54.713
What was that in reference to?

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:56.248
-I -- I never said that.

00:06:56.248 --> 00:06:59.118
-You didn't say that
on June 18th?

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:01.220
-No, I never said that.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.055
-Oh, wait a second.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:05.090
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.759
That's on me.
That was a Colbert joke.

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:09.061
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:11.264
-You like that joke?
-Yeah. That's a funny joke.

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:12.898
[ Applause ]
-That was a funny joke.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:13.966
Steve Higgins, everyone.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:16.702
No more questions!
No more questions!

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.770
Finally, listen to this --
A pair of Nike shoes

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:22.141
were just auctioned off
for a record $430,000.

00:07:22.141 --> 00:07:24.176
Can we see the shoes?
This is real.

00:07:24.176 --> 00:07:25.444
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:26.979
One day the buyer will show his
kids and say,

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:28.681
"These are the reason you
couldn't go to college."

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.882
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show.

